# Dedup env for TC-14 chain run.
#
# The committed dedup-14.env has two bugs that only matter for Docker:
#   * STATE_DIR_CONFIG=/tmp/dedup_state_13/ — copy-paste leftover from
#     TC-13's env file. Fixed here to _14 so a stale TC-13 state dir
#     can't leak stale gap-detector state into this test.
#   * BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=192.168.153.148:9092 — a bare-metal physical IP.
#     Harmless in Docker because docker-compose.yml's `dedup` service
#     sets BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS directly in `environment:`, which overrides
#     anything from this env_file (same key, environment: wins).
#
# GAP_EMIT_INTERVAL_SEC=5 / MISSING_REPORT_INTERVAL_SEC=5 (vs. the
# committed 60) — the chain only runs ~45 s end-to-end (phase 1 +
# post-drain create/resend + propagation wait), so a 60 s interval
# would emit at most once. We need several cycles: enough pre-resend
# cycles for `create` to see a populated `gaps` topic, and enough
# post-resend cycles for verify-tc14.sh to observe total_missing
# dropping back to 0.

WINDOW_SIZE=1000
MAX_WINDOWS=10
RAW_TOPICS=transfer
CLEAN_TOPIC=dedup
GAP_TOPIC=gaps
STATE_DIR_CONFIG=/tmp/dedup_state_14/
GAP_EMIT_INTERVAL_SEC=5
MISSING_REPORT_INTERVAL_SEC=5
PERSIST_INTERVAL_MS=10000
